{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"First, we note that $x=-\\dfrac13$ makes the denominator zero and so cannot be a solution.\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3x+1$ to get rid of the quotient. ","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{3x - 2}{3x + 1} \u0026= \\dfrac{1}{3}\n\\\\\\\\\n(3x+1)\\cdot \\dfrac{3x - 2}{3x + 1} \u0026= (3x+1)\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{3}\n\\\\\\\\\n3x-2\u0026=x+\\dfrac13\n\\\\\\\\\n2x\u0026=\\dfrac73\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=\\dfrac76\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We get that $x=\\dfrac76$ is a potential solution. It doesn't make the denominator zero, so it is indeed a solution.\n\n**In conclusion, $x=\\dfrac76$.**","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Solve for $x$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{3x - 2}{3x + 1} = \\dfrac{1}{3}$\n\n$x =$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"answerForms":["proper","improper"],"maxError":0,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":1.1666666666666667}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","multipleNumberInput":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
